            <div xml:id="d881">

                <pb facs="1159" n="1149" sameAs="frus:frus1946v10/pg1149"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">125.461/10–1746: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Stuart</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1946-10-24T15:00:00-05:00">October 24, 1946—3
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>925. Dept of opinion (Urtel 1679, Oct 17, 11 a.m.) we should not delay further
                    reopening Harbin and it is hoped final arrangements will be made for Clubb
                    proceeed there in near future. Details flight should be communicated to Chou
                    En-lai sufficiently in advance to enable him (Sent Nanking, repeated Mukden for
                    Clubb) notify local authorities Harbin.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
